    - target: {fileID: 5905881967701677635, guid: 3938ed1ae5c23814f8817ead1ed0d3bf, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: 'Property bindings allow you to map a variable value to a C# property.
        This allows you to easily use that value outside of the behavior tree and
        you do not need to worry about syncing the variable value. Properties must
        have both a getter and a setter in order for a variable to be able to bind
        to it.

        In this example the character has a Health variable that
        maps to the Health.Value property. See this page for more information:

        https://opsive.com/support/documentation/behavior-designer-pro/variables/property-bindings/'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
